# Changelog

## [0.6.1] - 2026-08-28

Commit range: `7662d16..6ecf9e3`

- Compute recorded duration from the union of the selected video asset
  layers' presentation ranges.
- Expose the exact presentation start, presentation end, and ending video
  packet id through the C and C++ duration-probe APIs.
- Preserve the first presentation timestamp as the start boundary even when
  later reordered samples have a lower timestamp.

## [0.6.0] - 2026-08-26

Commit range: `c9d9004..afda8b8`

- Add video transfer-characteristic metadata and HLG/PQ presentation hints.
- Add TLV transport parsing, resynchronization, and C API callbacks for IP
  flows, NTP, TLV-NIT, AMT, raw signalling tables, and unknown descriptors.
- Preserve MMTP timestamp, fragmentation, restart-offset, and damage evidence
  across malformed, truncated, and repositioned input.
- Split the demuxer test support into focused modules and extend transport,
  timestamp, colour, package, and C API coverage.

## [0.5.0] - 2026-08-16

Commit range: `d72b3d4..4b3853a`

- Expose the structured MH-EIT HDR programme icon and a positive-only video
  presentation hint without treating a missing icon as SDR.
- Add header-only HLG-to-SDR colour conversion and packed 3D LUT generation,
  including the calibrated BT.2446 prototype and numerical regression tests.
- Expose the LUT through the stable C API for direct FFmpeg integration.

## [0.4.0] - 2026-08-15

Commit range: `b807bd0..d72b3d4`

- Add reusable asset-layer helpers and discontinuity/damage spans for
  playback-recovery consumers.

## [0.3.0] (unreleased) - 2026-08-14

Commit range: `c712b1c..59204a3`

- Add video and asset-group metadata, a recording scanner, richer C API,
  pre-RAP seek handling, negative-PTS overflow protection, and selected-video
  packet/track controls.
- Add detailed subtitle track structures and document the extended subtitle
  metadata.

## [0.2.0] - 2026-08-11

Commit range: `91bafe3`

- Add duration probing and its test coverage.

## [0.1.1] - 2026-08-11

Commit range: `a8bbb0d..1ebeccb`

- Extract the ARIB MMT/TLV core as `libaribtlv`, validate the installed C++ API,
  and add a C API, documentation, tests, and relocatable pkg-config metadata.

## Core development before extraction - 2026-07-19 to 2026-08-04

Commit range: `050f800..3c6d800`

- Historical `tlvdemux` development that became the extracted core: MMT/TLV,
  compressed-IP and MMTP parsing, signalling, service selection, timestamps,
  audio descriptors, B62 subtitles, application/data assets, recording, and
  duration analysis.
